              "overview": "CSS selectors target elements for styling based on element type, class names, IDs, attributes, and structural tree relationships. Master the differences between universal (`*`), type, class (`.name`), ID (`#name`), descendant (space), child (`>`), and sibling combinators (`+`, `~`).",
